From: Frédéric Mahé <frederic.mahe@cirad.fr>
Subject: [PATCH] vsprintf: fix buffer overflow with PRINT_TIMESTAMP

vprintf() writes the timestamp prefix first, then formats the message
at &printbuffer[i] with the full buffer size, so a long message can
overflow printbuffer by up to the prefix length.

Signed-off-by: Frédéric Mahé <frederic.mahe@cirad.fr>
---
 lib/vsprintf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/vsprintf.c b/lib/vsprintf.c
--- a/lib/vsprintf.c
+++ b/lib/vsprintf.c
@@ -835,7 +835,7 @@ int vprintf(const char *fmt, va_list args)
 	 * For this to work, printbuffer must be larger than
 	 * anything we ever want to print.
 	 */
-	i += vscnprintf(&printbuffer[i], sizeof(printbuffer), fmt, args);
+	i += vscnprintf(&printbuffer[i], sizeof(printbuffer) - i, fmt, args);
 
 	/* Handle error */
 	if (i <= 0)
